"enwiki":"Buganda","summary":"Buganda is a Bantu kingdom within Uganda. The kingdom of the Baganda people, Buganda is the largest of the traditional kingdoms in present-day East Africa, consisting of Uganda's Central Region, including the Ugandan capital Kampala. The 14 million Baganda (singular Muganda; often referred to simply by the root word and adjective, Ganda) make up the largest Ugandan region, representing approximately 16% of Uganda's population.\nBuganda's history includes unification around the 13th century by the first king, Kato Kintu, the founder of Buganda's Kintu dynasty, and Buganda grew to become one of the largest and most powerful states in East Africa during the 18th and the 19th centuries."}],"facts":[{"qid":"Q473748","kind":"capital","value_qid":"Q3894","value_label":"Kampala","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P36","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Kampala"},{"qid":"Q473748","kind":"official_language","value_qid":"Q33368","value_label":"Luganda","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P37","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Luganda"},{"qid":"Q473748","kind":"language","value_qid":"Q33368","value_label":"Luganda","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P2936","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Luganda"},{"qid":"Q473748","kind":"successor","value_qid":"Q101048575","value_label":"Bouganda","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P1366","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Bouganda"},{"qid":"Q473748","kind":"flag","value_qid":null,"value_label":"Flag of Buganda.svg","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P41","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":null}],"people":{},"media":{"Flag of Buganda.svg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Flag_of_Buganda.svg/330px-Flag_of_Buganda.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Buganda.svg","author":"Mysid","license":"Public domain"}},"names":["Ba